      "title": "Cochrane Systematic Review: Shengmai for Heart Failure (2014, updated from 2012)",
      "description": "This Cochrane review included 14 RCTs with 858 patients. Adding Shengmai preparations to standard treatment improved heart function classification (NYHA) compared to usual treatment alone, with benefits also seen in ejection fraction, cardiac output, and exercise capacity. However, the quality of evidence was rated low due to small sample sizes and methodological limitations. More rigorous trials were recommended.",
